 "description": "Financial statements of one company from the XBRL data in its 10-K, 10-Q, 20-F and 40-F filings (SEC companyfacts), newest period first: income statement (revenue, cost_of_revenue, gross_profit, operating_expenses, rd_expense, sga_expense, operating_income, interest_expense, tax_expense, net_income, eps_basic, eps_diluted, shares_basic, shares_diluted), balance sheet (cash_and_equivalents ... total_assets, total_liabilities, total_equity including minority interest), cash flow (operating_cash_flow, capex, free_cash_flow = operating cash flow minus capex, dividends_paid, share_buybacks, ..., depreciation_amortization, stock_based_compensation) and the cover-page shares outstanding (shares, with change_1y_pct). period=annual gives fiscal years (FY), quarterly gives single fiscal quarters (Q1-Q4). IMPORTANT: amounts are in the company's reporting currency (`currency`, for example TWD for TSMC), not US dollars; for other currencies usd_rate gives US dollars per unit: multiply income statement and cash flow amounts by usd_rate.average and balance sheet amounts by usd_rate.period_end. EPS is in that currency per share. Each period has its filing (form, filed_date, accession, sec_url), reported_date (the earnings 8-K, Item 2.02), margins (gross, operating and net margin, stock-based compensation as a percent of revenue) and yoy_pct (growth against the same fiscal period a year earlier). Numbers are as filed in each period's original report or its amendment. Known gaps: foreign companies (20-F, 40-F) have annual statements only; EPS and share counts are not adjusted for stock splits (stock_splits lists the splits in the range); for ADRs EPS is per ordinary share, not per ADS; Q4 and single-quarter cash flows are mostly derived by subtraction (listed in derived); banks' revenue may be interest income only; companies with several share classes may have no EPS or cover-page share count. `note` explains what applies to this company, including why there are no statements (ETFs and funds have none). No stock prices are returned and no valuation ratios are computed; get_stock has the company's market cap in USD (convert foreign-currency statements with usd_rate before comparing).",
 "inputSchema": {
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "properties": {
   "limit": {
    "description": "Number of periods, newest first: default 5 for annual, 8 for quarterly, at most 40.",
    "maximum": 40,
    "minimum": 1,
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "period": {
    "default": "annual",
    "description": "annual = fiscal years (default); quarterly = single fiscal quarters.",
    "enum": [
     "annual",
     "quarterly"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "statements": {
    "description": "Which parts to return: income, balance, cash_flow, shares (cover-page shares outstanding). Default all, e.g. [\"income\"].",
    "items": {
     "enum": [
      "income",
      "balance",
      "cash_flow",
      "shares"
     ],
     "type": "string"
    },
    "maxItems": 4,
    "minItems": 1,
    "type": "array"
   },
   "ticker": {
    "description": "Stock ticker, e.g. AAPL or BRK.B (share classes use a dot; BRK-B also works).",
    "maxLength": 12,
    "minLength": 1,
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "ticker"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
